<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constans II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">630–668</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Constantine the Bearded</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Constans II was Byzantine emperor from 641 to 668, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-muslim-conquests">Arab conquests</a> that took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and threatened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. He moved his court west in 663, campaigned against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and resided at Syracuse in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, strengthening Byzantine positions there, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>. He was murdered in his bath at Syracuse in 668.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constans-ii.jpg" alt="Constans II" width="320" height="312" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown; Image: Classical Numismatic Group, Inc.. CNG allows the use of any of their images as long as they are attri... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Solidus_Constans_II_(obverse).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
